          "body": "The forest's solid crowns, discontinuous weapon poses and detached global-time slash weakened the whole scene. This unit replaces tree crowns with photographed branch cutouts, keeps the saved combat pose continuous with fixed-length two-hand grips, and draws a bounded tapered trail from the actual weapon transform.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #39 while GitHub reports its normal merge operation still in progress. It must be retargeted to main after #39 actually merges; do not merge it into the feature branch or bypass the required checks.\n\nPoly Haven CC0 source maps and provenance are retained. Only two 512 RGBA PNGs, 327,978 B total, enter the lazy scene. The same 805 tree placements, collisions, gameplay clocks, saves, title movie, audio and UI are preserved.\n\nAll 18 required local commands and 242 tests passed in 76.663 s. Independent actual SceneView/Game integration preserves returned forest textures across near/far color and shadow passes, detects missing installation, checks 99/99 release updates at three scene rates against fixed 60 Hz simulation, and matches 407 same-frame blade coordinate checks exactly. Pauses, death, teleports and new game clear trail history. Initial JS stays 163,175 B under the existing 165,000 B gate with three chunks. Standalone is 13,576,431 B, SHA256 9c80c6c5e68e20b40ef2d143874d5e6a4f7c3215e94317df37c4b20856212507; the remote tree exactly matches tested c7c1d436e7ca7a8777fec57007aff61c3cdc34dd.\n\nThe renderer and texture loaders are explicit boundaries in the Node integration check. This is not WebGL, actual device/FPS, audio listening or PS4 perceptual acceptance. Documentation records actual source images, geometry/motion comparisons, review fixes, asset budgets, unavailable evidence and the next substantive quality work. Production continues beyond this finite unit.",
